    {
      "text": "####mapPartitions\n*Spark operates on a per-partition basis when it comes to\nactually executing code. You also might have noticed earlier that the return signature of a map\nfunction on an RDD is actually MapPartitionsRDD. This is because map is just a row-wise alias\nfor mapPartitions, which makes it possible for you to map an individual partition (represented\nas an iterator)*",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "99410f2429df42d499f30"
    },
    {
      "text": "%spark\nwords.getNumPartitions",
      "config": {
