      "id": "5060e85984324d79b2782"
    },
    {
      "text": "###Transformation on RDD\n\n1. distinct: take the distinct value\n2. filter: filter the row\n3. map: *Specify a function that returns the value that you want, given the correct input. You then apply that, record by record*\n4. flatMap: *flatMap provides a simple extension of the map function we just looked at. Sometimes, each current row should return multiple rows*\n5. sortBy: words.sortBy(row => row.length * -1)\n\n###Action\n1. collect: *collect the data on the driver*\n2. count:\n3. countByValue: *words.countByValue() You should use this method only if the resulting map is expected to be small because the entire thing is loaded into the driver’s memory.*\n3. reduce:  *words.reduce((x,y) => if(x.length > y.length) x else y)  //longest words*\n4. redcuceByKey: *require key.value pair\n5. *words.first()*\n6. min : *spark.sparkContext.parallelize(1 to 20).min()*\n7. max: *spark.sparkContext.parallelize(1 to 20).max()*\n8. words.saveAsTextFile(\"file:/tmp/bookTitle\")\n\n",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "e1cec1a68ba6442e93064"
    },
    {
      "text": "%spark\n//rdd\nval flightRdd:RDD[String] = spark\n.sparkContext\n.textFile(\"dbfs:/FileStore/tables/suankiData/raw/flightData/2011_summary.csv\")\n\nval firstRow = flightRdd.first\n\nval flightRdd1 =\n flightRdd\n .filter(row => row !=firstRow && !row.trim.contains(\"Eustatius\"))\n\n\n val finalflightRdd=flightRdd1.map(row => row.split(\",\"))\n\n\n\n",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/scala",
        "editorSetting": {
